# Known HIGH/CRITICAL npm advisories in integrations/solana-agent-kit/package-lock.json.
# Read by gate.mjs in the CI supply-chain job. One `GHSA-id@package` per line
# (the advisory in that package only); the rest of the line is a note. A new advisory fails CI; so does a listed one that is
# no longer reported (prune it in the change that fixes it).
#
# Recorded 2026-09-30. At 3327fcf this tree carried 36 distinct high/critical
# advisories (3 critical). 35 are gone:
#   - The bridge no longer loads @solana-agent-kit/plugin-defi or plugin-token
#     (it never called them; importing one ran its whole dependency tree in
#     the process holding the private key). That removed the Drift, OKX,
#     Meteora, Orca, Pyth and Switchboard trees: 25 advisories, all three
#     criticals.
#   - package.json `overrides` force patched versions inside the same major
#     line where the parent had not moved: fast-uri 3.1.8, nanoid 3.3.19,
#     jsondiffpatch 0.7.6, langsmith 0.6.3, hono 4.13.12, ip-address 10.7.2,
#     qs 6.16.0. Typecheck and all bridge tests pass on them.
#
# What remains has no fix that can be applied from here:
GHSA-3gc7-fjrx-p6mg@bigint-buffer  # high  bigint-buffer <=1.1.5 (no patched release exists): solana-agent-kit 2.0.10 -> @solana/spl-token 0.4.15 -> @solana/buffer-layout-utils 0.3.0 -> bigint-buffer 1.1.5 (npm ls, 2026-10-02). The overflow is in the package's NATIVE addon (toBigIntLE). Every install of this tree runs with --ignore-scripts, so the addon is never built and bigint-buffer runs its pure-JS fallback. Moving the bridge's own code to @solana/kit does not remove it; dropping the solana-agent-kit dependency does (roadmap gap R-P8, phase 3).
#
# Below the gate's threshold, recorded for completeness:
#   - stream-json (moderate) and uuid (moderate) come through jayson, web3.js
#     1.x's own HTTP RPC client. The uuid advisory needs a caller-supplied
#     output buffer, which jayson never passes. Forcing uuid across three
#     majors into web3.js was judged riskier than the advisory.
#   - ai <5.0.52 and @ai-sdk/provider-utils <3.0.28 (low): fixed only in the
#     ai 5 line, which solana-agent-kit 2.x does not use.
